# Testing Patterns

> Test structure and conventions for {{project.name}}.

## When to Use

Load this skill when writing any tests — unit, integration, or component tests.

## Test Structure

```typescript
describe('[ModuleName]', () => {
  describe('[functionName]', () => {
    it('should [expected behavior] when [condition]', () => {
      // Arrange
      // Act
      // Assert
    });
  });
});
```

## Naming Convention

- Test files: `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx`
- Describe blocks: module or class name
- It blocks: `should [verb] when [condition]`

## Key Rules

- Each test must be independent — no shared mutable state
- Use `beforeEach` for setup, not `beforeAll` (unless expensive)
- Mock external dependencies (database, APIs, file system)
- Test both happy paths and error cases
- Test boundary conditions (empty arrays, null values, max values)
- One assertion concept per test (multiple expects are OK if related)

